Fonts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The window draws text with the faces `egui` bundles, reached through the
`epaint_default_fonts` crate and carried inside the Mochi executable. They are
not Mochi's work and both licences ask that they be named:

  Ubuntu Light            Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0
                          https://ubuntu.com/legal/font-licence
  Hack                    SIL Open Font Licence 1.1 (and a Bitstream Vera
                          derivative notice)
                          https://github.com/source-foundry/Hack
  Noto Emoji, emoji-icon  SIL Open Font Licence 1.1
                          https://github.com/googlefonts/noto-emoji

Neither licence restricts Mochi's own licence, and neither font is modified.

For text those faces do not cover — Japanese, Chinese and Korean — Mochi reads
a font the operating system already has (Yu Gothic, Meiryo, Hiragino, Noto CJK
and so on, see `crates/mochi-gui/src/fonts.rs`). Nothing of that font is copied
into the executable or redistributed: it is read at startup from the machine it
is already installed on.

A machine-generated inventory of the exact dependency versions and their
licences is produced by `cargo deny list` and is published with each release.
When a new dependency introduces its own NOTICE requirements, its attribution
must be appended to this file (Apache-2.0 section 4(d)).
